      "lede": null,
      "objectives": [],
      "sections": [
        {
          "id": "connect-foundations-t17-s1",
          "eyebrow": null,
          "duration": null,
          "title": "Overview",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "To improve customer experience, you need to measure it effectively. The following are key metrics and methods for evaluating customer experience in contact centers."
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "To learn more, choose the START or arrow buttons to display each of the six steps."
            },
            {
              "type": "h",
              "level": 4,
              "text": "Measuring resolution efficiency"
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "By measuring key performance indicators, you can continuously improve your operations. Have you considered tracking interactions across various channels with Amazon Connect's analytics capabilities?"
            },
            {
              "type": "h",
              "level": 4,
              "text": "CSAT"
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "Customer satisfaction (CSAT) measures how satisfied customers are with a specific interaction. When setting up CSAT surveys, consider the following best practices:"
            },
            {
              "type": "ul",
              "items": [
                "It's typical to use a five-point scale (very satisfied to very dissatisfied).",
                "Collect <X> through post-call surveys, emails, or text messages.",
                "Provide immediate feedback on specific interactions."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "With Amazon Connect, you can implement post-call surveys by using flows to automatically collect CSAT data after interactions."
            },
            {
              "type": "h",
              "level": 4,
              "text": "NPS"
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "Net promoter score (NPS) measures customer loyalty by asking how likely customers are to recommend your company. NPS surveys typically include the following characteristics:"
            },
            {
              "type": "ul",
              "items": [
                "Uses a 0–10 scale.",
                "Categorizes customers as promoters (9–10), passives (7–8), or detractors (0–6)."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "To calculate the net promoter score, subtract the percentage of detractors from the percentage of promoters collected by the survey. The NPS result is typically expressed as an integer rather than a percentage."
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "NPS is valuable for understanding long-term customer loyalty beyond individual interactions."
            },
            {
              "type": "h",
              "level": 4,
              "text": "Customer effort score"
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "Customer effort score (CES) measures the effort a customer expends to get their issue resolved or a question answered. To assess this, organizations typically do the following:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "connect-foundations-t17-s2",
          "eyebrow": null,
          "duration": null,
          "title": "Ask customers, \"How efficient was your issue resolution today?\"",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "Uses a scale ranging from very inefficient to very efficient."
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "Tracks responses to predict future purchase behavior and loyalty."
            },
            {
              "type": "h",
              "level": 4,
              "text": "FCR"
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "First contact resolution (FCR) tracks how often customer issues are resolved in the initial interaction. It is a key metric for customer service because it indicates the effectiveness of a call center's ability to address customer needs efficiently and quickly. Measuring resolution success includes the following:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "connect-foundations-t17-s3",
          "eyebrow": null,
          "duration": null,
          "title": "Using Amazon Connect Contact Lens to identify repeat contacts",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "h",
              "level": 4,
              "text": "Customer conversation analysis"
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "Amazon Connect dashboard showing sentiment trend, sentiment distribution, and talk time analysis."
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "Amazon Connect Contact Lens analyzes customer conversations beyond surveys. Contact Lens can do the following:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "connect-foundations-t17-s4",
          "eyebrow": null,
          "duration": null,
          "title": "Detect emerging trends before they appear in survey data",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "The following sentiment analyses can be viewed in Amazon Connect:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "connect-foundations-t17-s5",
          "eyebrow": null,
          "duration": null,
          "title": "Talk time",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "h",
              "level": 4,
              "text": "Customer journey analytics"
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "Customer journey analytics helps understand customer experience across multiple interactions and touchpoints. It helps evaluate customer experience in the following ways:"
            },
            {
              "type": "ul",
              "items": [
                "Track paths that customers take across channels.",
                "Identify common drop-off points or friction areas.",
                "Compare and analyze successful and unsuccessful journeys."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "h",
              "level": 4,
              "text": "Summary"
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "Amazon Connect provides the tools to implement effective customer experience strategies. Several methods can help accomplish this evaluation process effectively. These include implementing automated post-call surveys, utilizing advanced Contact Lens analytics for sentiment analysis, and leveraging Customer Profiles for detailed customer journey mapping."
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "By collecting, analyzing, and acting on this customer experience data, you can create a continuous improvement cycle for your customer experience strategies. Amazon Connect equips you with the ability to consistently elevate service quality, increase customer loyalty, and deliver measurable business results."
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "The goal is not only measurement, but using these insights to drive meaningful actions. These actions help enhance customer experience, empower agents, and align contact center operations with broader business objectives."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
